///
/// The Ink/Graphite token table (design appendix section 4.2): one row per
/// `llmfun::tui::ui::ColorToken`, in declaration order.
///
///   rgb              the design's sRGB colour + alpha (`TrueColor`)
///   xterm256         the colour to APPLY at 256 colours, packed as IM_COL32
///   xterm256Index    the xterm-256 entry the terminal paints for it
///   ansi16           the colour to apply at 16 colours, packed as IM_COL32
///   ansi16Index      the base colour it names
///
/// The applied colour is a pre-image of the entry, not the entry itself: imtui
/// quantizes the style colour again (`rgbToAnsi256`), and palette entries are
/// not fixed points of that formula - applying the entry would show a different
/// colour than `xterm256Index` promises. `tools/gen_tokens.py` proves the round
/// trip for every row before writing it, and `test_tokens` re-proves it.
///
/// Regenerate with `python3 tools/gen_tokens.py`; `--check` fails when this file
/// and the script disagree, or when the token order no longer matches
/// `cpp_tui/ui/tokens.h`.
